diagnosis_text:
The helpdesk report that PC11 (172.16.20.11, VLAN 20) is "completely isolated" is not confirmed by any live evidence. Phase 1 reachability probing shows PC11 successfully pinging hosts on two distinct remote subnets — pc12 at 172.16.30.12 (0% loss) and pc3 at 10.6.0.3 (0% loss) — both of which require traversal through its default gateway at 172.16.20.254. This directly refutes the claim that PC11 cannot reach its gateway or any remote subnet.

A full broad-search pass (Phases A through D) found no mechanism that could produce isolation: infra_sweep confirms all 15 hosts including PC11 hold valid IPv4 addresses and default routes with no gateway or resolver divergence; l2_snapshot finds zero duplicate MACs; ospf_snapshot shows all nine FRR routers in Full adjacency with 18 routes apiece and every OSPF interface in a healthy state; tc_snapshot finds no shaping qdiscs on any network-path interface; pressure_sweep identifies no stress tools, CPU pressure, or socket floods on any device. There is no flap script, no carrier-transition history, no ACL drop rule, and no ARP anomaly that could explain a historical isolation event either.

Root cause: No fault exists. PC11's switch port, VLAN membership, IP addressing, gateway reachability, and inter-subnet routing are all operating correctly at the time of investigation. The user report is unconfirmed and inconsistent with current live measurements.

Fix: No corrective action is required. If the user experiences future outages, a timestamped reachability capture at the moment of the complaint would be needed to identify any transient fault.
=== END ===